# EMDR — marketing section spacing (centered heads)

When a marketing band has a **centered title + sub** above cards/grid/content (e.g. `/pricing` plans, similar hubs):

## Do this

1. **Clear the overlay header** — `.frontend-header--overlay` / `.frontend-header-pill` sits on top of the page. `padding-top` on the section must put the H1/H2 **below** the pill with ~2.5–3.5rem air (measure: `titleTop > pillBottom + ~40px`). Do not guess from “looks fine” while the title underlaps the header hit box.
2. **Separate head from content with flex `gap`** — on the section’s `.fe-container` (or equivalent wrapper):

```css
.section > .fe-container {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: stretch;
  gap: clamp(3.5rem, 6vw, 5rem); /* title/sub → cards */
}

.section .fe-pricing-head /* or .fe-section-head */ {
  margin: 0 auto; /* kill global margin: 0 auto clamp(...) */
  max-width: /* as designed */;
}
```

3. **Equal rhythm** — roughly match:
   - air under the pill → title
   - gap under title/sub → content
   - padding under the content band

4. **Override shared section chrome** — global rules like `.fe-pricing-section { padding: … }` or `.fe-pricing-head { margin: 0 auto clamp(…) }` will fight page-specific layout. Use higher specificity (and `!important` on padding only when a shorthand elsewhere wins) scoped to the page modifier (e.g. `.fe-pricing-section--page`).

## Do not

| Bad | Why |
|---|---|
| Only `margin-bottom` on the head | Collapses / loses to global `.fe-pricing-head { margin: 0 auto clamp }` |
| Tiny `padding-top` under overlay (~5–7rem) | Title sits under the pill; looks “cramped under header” |
| `min-height: 100svh` + `justify-content: center` for this job | Uneven air above/below when content height varies |
| Card hover lift (`translateY`) eating the gap under the sub | Lift eats the trial→cards air — lift only if grid has compensating `padding-top` |

